WEBVTT

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:12.250
So you're saying you won't accept our 
conditions under any circumstance?

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.040
No! We didn't mean to give you that impression—

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.170
This is tedious.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:20.490
We're not deleting anything Lupin's written 
on PeopleLog, nor anything by anyone else.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.370
But if Lupin keeps posting like he is, 
it's only going to aggravate the situation.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.000
His posts have already been responsible

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.380
for a presidential race where 
every single candidate withdrew!

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.370
A string of posts on 
fraudulent accounting

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.390
has left every stock market 
in the world in chaos!

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.880
And claims he made about international 
trade have torpedoed existing deals!

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:45.030
The world's been brought to 
its knees because of Lupin's lies!

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.840
Except they're <i>not</i> lies, are they?

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.400
PeopleLog's giving them all A-ratings.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.640
And that's the problem!

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.650
It's like PeopleLog is approving 
everything Lupin says!

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.670
Sounds to me like you need 
to stop having secrets

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.980
that get you into trouble 
when Lupin makes them public.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.660
If you all stopped being shady, 
the world would be a better place.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.850
That's part of the future 
our app is trying to create.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.160
Is something funny?

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.180
And yet, even PeopleLog couldn't 
predict what Lupin was going to do.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.300
You're going to need more than 
just data to understand that guy.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.400
So where have you been for the past month?

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.420
Oh, you know, traveling 
around, visiting old friends.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.710
Not <i>female</i> friends, I hope.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.930
Perish the thought!

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.820
For all the enemies this guy has, 
he has just as many allies.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.690
A rogues' gallery that no 
machine could ever predict.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.480
I gotta ask, though. What's with the trawler?

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.770
Oh, it's my way of going incognito.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.780
Well, you know how I'm 
<i>super</i> famous and all that?

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.980
There are times I just wanna get 
away from prying eyes, y'know?

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.480
I get you.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.750
Nothing good comes from 
being a celebrity, if you ask me.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.730
I got a bite.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.440
Now, then, we've got a calling card to send.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.020
Why did you break up with Lupin?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.440
Because we were going out.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.520
Stop joking around.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.190
I'm being serious.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.200
Are you stupid or something?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.280
Well, I couldn't let you die alone, could I?

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:06.290
Guess not. If this really is the end,

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.510
maybe I should find a nice guy 
to settle down with...

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:10.280
I wonder who I'll pick...

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.290
Aw, don't be like that. Besides, 
I'm the only one up here with you.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.300
Well... looks like I don't 
have a choice, then, do I?

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.370
I'm not sure what made me say yes to him.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.830
I mean, it was fun living together.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:36.910
Getting up at the same time, 
going to bed together...

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.670
Sharing meals and drinks...

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.890
We even went furniture shopping together.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:41.800
But...

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.150
Did you have a fight?

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.960
Over another woman maybe?

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:47.110
Nothing broke us up.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.550
Then, why <i>did</i> you break up?

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.200
Like I said, nothing did.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:55.340
I don't do riddles.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.030
No excitement, no thrills...

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.080
No romantic cat-and-mouse, 
no death-defying heists...

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:03.690
Zilcho.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.340
I suppose settling down just didn't suit us.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.850
So what does suit you?

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.840
I'd love to know that myself.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.410
What do <i>you</i> want?

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.870
Lupin's vanished.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.400
PeopleLog's functioning how it's meant to.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.290
So that means there's
 not enough data on him.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.870
Lupin has some kind of secret.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.210
Something the world doesn't know...

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.870
Something huge!

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.390
Enzo!

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.530
China's following the EU's lead, 
 talking about sanctions!

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.880
We need to start softening our stance!

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.080
No!

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.900
Removing human subjectivity 
is what makes PeopleLog

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.630
an app that can correct 
humanity's prejudices and ignorance!

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.890
That's just idealistic!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:08.150
I thought we were trying to 
make those ideals a reality.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.160
Well...

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:17.660
What was <i>that</i>?

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:28.660
<i>My fellow Americans.</i>

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.170
<i>Following discussions with 
our allies, I have ordered</i>

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:37.180
<i>military strikes on the 
Shake Hands corporation.</i>

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:42.380
Not only does their PeopleLog program 
infringe on our right to privacy,

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.960
it also represents a grave 
threat to our national security.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.390
<i>Their intention to unravel 
our democracy is clear,</i>

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:52.420
<i>and even though Shakes Hands 
may call themselves a business,</i>

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:55.260
<i>they will now be classified 
as a terrorist organization.</i>

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.310
What's he talking about?!

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.400
We're terrorists?!

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.810
We haven't even done anything illegal!

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.060
W-We need to give ourselves up!

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.330
What the hell is the boss <i>doing</i>?!

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.800
Why's this happening?

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.350
This isn't what we agreed!

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:12.090
You promised to keep military action 
off the table as long as PeopleLog—

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:15.100
You're right. I did make that promise.

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:18.090
And now... I've broken it.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.000
He played you, Ling.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.300
Which is why PeopleLog 
couldn't predict this attack.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.840
Let's get outta here, Enzo!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.500
If we go through the tunnels 
the network cables use...

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.760
By all means, go.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:33.610
Enzo?

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:38.360
You've never had faith 
in the app we created.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.870
Looks like I might not have time 
to wait for Lupin, after all.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.390
Fujiko... Lupin's posted a calling card.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.260
<b>Arriving Today</b>

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.010
That's Lupin for you! The master thief!

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.010
Lupin III is here, here, here, here!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:51.800
Yo, it's Lupin III time!!!

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:53.640
Lupin sent a calling card! 
About damn time!

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.410
<b>Sushi</b>

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:54.820
Yata!

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.390
Yessir! Right behind you!

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.540
Never mind that nonsense.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.780
No thief is going to make a difference—

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:02.800
Picking up a vessel on sonar.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:03.390
What?

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:04.910
It's a submersible!

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:20.660
I owe you one, Diana!

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:26.170
Well, I was indebted to you for 
that business with my grandfather.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:31.020
"Thieves are in the shadows. 
All's right with the world."

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:35.420
<i>To all the folks who were 
looking for me: Nice try!</i>

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:36.920
Lupin!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.920
And now, to save all of you the trouble,

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.940
you're about to be treated to 
a live stream of a Lupin III heist!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:45.120
Goemon.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:45.930
Understood.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.200
Bullseye!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.930
All right!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.930
Dammit!

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.950
You guys are rootin' for Lupin?

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.090
Lupin's the best there ever was!

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:03.220
Yeah, what he said!

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:08.720
Show 'em what for!

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.070
I'm on Lupin's side, too!

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.030
You're cheerleadin' for the crook?

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.470
What the <i>hell</i> did you say?

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.970
<b>Yakitori</b>

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.970
Cats & Dogs

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:25.380
What the...

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:33.420
Get some distance!

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.560
Lupin, we shall handle this!

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.160
You're gonna go have some 
face-time with Fujiko, right?

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.700
Good idea. Think I will.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.470
You think we can take these guys?

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:05.210
There is nothing duller than 
a battle where the outcome is certain.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.500
No arguments there.

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:13.530
They're not running...

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:19.320
Just you watch what human legs can do!

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:21.700
<i>The enemy's putting up stiff resistance!</i>

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.340
<i>We're having a hard time getting in!</i>

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.570
They have a PMC?

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.520
What kind of enemy force are we looking at?

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.340
<i>There are... two of them, sir.</i>

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.450
<i>Two enemies. A gunman and a samurai.</i>

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:33.330
What? The hell are you talking about?!

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.220
Goemon!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:46.390
That's impossible!!!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:46.390
That's crazy!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:46.390
That's one cool samurai

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:46.390
Is this real life?

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.600
No way... This has to be CGI

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:49.360
Guys like this can't actually exist

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.190
But PeopleLog's 
giving it an A-rating...

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.690
Look, Mother. It's Jigen.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.260
Go get 'em, Goemon!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.440
You can do it!

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.950
I'm on my way, princesses!

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:27.270
Enzo! Dammit, Enzo!

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:32.470
Did you seriously think we didn't
 know about these tunnels?

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:42.000
Yes. Negotiations have failed.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.480
Enzo's in the wind.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.360
Ling got caught up in the strikes.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.360
I've confirmed that he's dead.

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:52.300
I'm personally bringing you in 
and putting your talents to use.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:56.180
PeopleLog's tech will come in very handy 
when I want to control a country.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:59.180
You're going to betray your nation?

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:02.840
They'll be better off 
with me running the show

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.520
than leaders who change 
every time there's an election.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:09.830
All right.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.520
I've stolen what I came for, Lupin.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.010
What about you?

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:26.420
It's no good. The fire suppression 
systems won't be able to handle this.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.660
The building's going to come 
crashing down within the hour!

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.520
Lupin... Are you okay?

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:39.710
Is the camera acting up?

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:42.590
C'mon! Work! This is the good bit!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.210
Is there too much traffic?

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.720
No. This is...

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:51.720
It's Lupin!

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.760
He's taken administrative access.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.740
What the hell is the 
countermeasure team doing?

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:07.240
Don't think you can bring PeopleLog 
down with your little pranks!

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.780
It can't be...

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:21.750
Lupin!

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:27.510
You climbed the elevator 
cable to get up here?

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:31.750
Well? Looks like PeopleLog isn't 
as omniscient as you thought.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:35.010
And you came all this way just to prove that?

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:37.700
Yep. And because, Fujiko...

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:40.520
...I wanted to prove I'm not gonna die.

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:44.020
That's enough nonsense out of you!

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.250
Lupin!

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:48.950
Spill it, Lupin!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.260
You <i>must</i> have some kind of secret.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:54.900
You couldn't possibly have 
evaded PeopleLog without one.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.740
Put the gun down!

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:57.910
What?

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.640
Don't do this. I can't shoot you.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:05.250
And why's that? Did PeopleLog 
tell you that you couldn't?

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:11.710
You think you can write an all-knowing app 
when you don't even know your own daughter?!

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:14.260
Well, there's already blood on my hands!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.260
It's okay, Amy.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:20.240
Don't worry. He's not gonna shoot.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.350
But...

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.680
Enzo here is just curious.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.140
He wants to know what I'll say next.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.800
What I'll do next.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:34.300
Because unless it can figure me out, 
your PeopleLog app will never be perfect.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.200
Fujiko.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:44.040
I love you.

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:45.780
I know.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.290
You are the most radiant woman in the world.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.160
I know that, too.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.250
You want me to answer your question 
from the other day, don't you?

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:58.800
Yes, I do, Lupin.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.550
What am I to you?

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:02.790
Your lover?

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:03.990
Your rival?

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:05.400
An obstacle?

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.330
A stepping stone?

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:07.830
A port in a storm?

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.230
Or am I supposed to be your coffin?

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:14.270
If we were both men, 
I'd be fine with just being friends.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:18.840
But I don't really believe men 
and women can just be friends.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:22.450
Y'know, I've been thinking 
about it for a while now.

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:24.990
About a <i>lot</i> of stuff... 
ever since you asked me that.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.830
Thing is... I still don't 
know, to be honest.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:31.050
"Who is Lupin III, really?"

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:32.970
Running away again?

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:37.400
And after thinking it through,

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.730
this is the best answer 
I could come up with.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.260
Lupin?!

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:56.880
That's it, Lupin! That's how you did it!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:00.610
It's collapsing!

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:04.180
Amy, you've gotta analyze 
the construction of the building!

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.610
Then, simulate how it's gonna fall,

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.490
and find out which bit's going 
to be the last bit standing!

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.790
Hello, Underworld!

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:16.690
That was you?

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.390
Lupin!

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:22.610
Wait, Jigen!

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.560
Angle looks good!

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.080
Let's fly!

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:39.370
The analysis is complete.

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:41.270
We've got 32 seconds until 
it collapses completely.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.970
So we've gotta hit the ground first!

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:44.480
Lupin!

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:47.530
I know your secret now!

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:50.370
My next iteration of PeopleLog 
will catch you, for sure!

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:53.270
You seriously think that's the only 
secret I've got up my sleeve?

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:54.900
Lupin III has plenty more where—

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:02.380
Lupin!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.390
You've got to be kidding me!

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:13.720
Amy, over here!

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:16.270
Amy!

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.610
It's not Amy! It's Ami!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.910
Everyone calls me Amy.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:27.740
Why did you give me 
such a hard name to say?

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.760
It's a word from your Mom's country!

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.790
It means "net"!

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:38.660
We came up with it together.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:43.300
Your name connects to the future!

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.670
Dammit. It's a war zone down there!

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.000
Sir... I think Lupin might—

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.210
Lupin will <i>not</i> die!

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.500
He won't die before I've caught him.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.200
I refuse to let him die.

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:50.230
Lupin! You're under arrest!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:56.770
Hey, it's Pops.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.840
Great. Trouble just keeps finding us.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:18:59.660
Indeed.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:01.380
Lupin, we're gonna go on ahead.

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:02.280
Hey!

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:05.480
Fujiko...

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:07.100
Well, Amy.

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:08.740
You coming with?

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.380
Thanks for everything, Lupin.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.780
I'll see you around.

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:31.140
All right. Until next time, Amy!

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:37.890
Are you sure about this?

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:42.690
I want to be near him, 
but if I'm too close, I get restless.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.860
I want him to be mine,

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:48.530
but if I had him all to myself, 
I'd only be disappointed.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.500
I want to know everything about him,

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.040
but I still want him to surprise me...

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:55.910
What do you call someone like that?

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:01.420
You really want to know what 
people like that are called, Ami?

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.060
You know?

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:07.620
They're heroes.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:15.660
Yeah!

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:34.560
So you were able to shut down 
PeopleLog, right, Lupin?!

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.840
He says he's gonna make another one!

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.100
Say what?!

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:39.840
Even if we put Enzo out of action,

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:42.850
there's gonna be plenty of people 
with the same idea down the line!

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:45.910
The world has truly become 
a troublesome place.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:47.720
What's that? You're gonna retire?

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:52.020
Perhaps I shall. I <i>did</i> defeat you, after all.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.580
It's best two out of three!

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.510
We're fighting again, Goemon!

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:58.340
The first serious duel between 
men settles the matter.

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:01.660
Get back here, Lupin!

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.370
You're under arrest!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.370
He never changes!

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:07.360
And neither do we!

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:09.360
But that is a good thing.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.370
Hey, it works for me!

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.770
To Amy

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.270
I'm going to keep you two safe. 
Go on ahead and wait at my apartment.

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:44.950
<b>Viva Lupin III</b>
